<p>Minutes stretched into hours. The colony remained in a state of suspended animation, two factions staring at each other across a invisible line. Patricia had control of the security forces and the shuttle bay. Chen had control of the communications center, the medical wing, and the loyalty of most of the civilian population.</p>

<p>Then Yuki's call came. "It works. The first patient is showing signs of neurological recovery. Nanite activity has ceased. Neural pathways are beginning to regenerate."</p>

<p>Elena felt a surge of hope so powerful it nearly brought her to her knees. "How long until you can treat everyone?"</p>

<p>"I need to build more devices. With the resources available, I can treat ten patients per hour. All forty-seven affected colonists can be treated within five hours."</p>

<p>"Start immediately. Priority goes to the most severe cases."</p>

<p>"Understood."</p>

<p>Elena turned to Chen, her voice stronger than it had been in days. "We have a treatment. We can save everyone."</p>

<p>Chen's eyes glistened. "Then we have a future. Patricia can run, but she can't hide from what we've built."</p>

<p>"She's still trying to escape. We need to stop her."</p>

