<p>"Elena, you're a doctor—"</p>

<p>"I'm also a colonist. And I'm not going to let Patricia Okonkwo destroy everything we've built."</p>

<p>She left the communications center and moved through the corridors toward the shuttle bay. The colony was eerily quiet, the usual hum of activity replaced by tense silence. Doors were sealed. Lights were dimmed. Everyone was waiting.</p>

<p>She reached the access corridor to the shuttle bay and found it blocked by two security officers. They saw her and raised their weapons. "Dr. Vasquez. You're under arrest by order of Acting Governor Okonkwo."</p>

<p>Elena raised her hands, the sidearm hidden behind her back. "I'm not here to fight. I'm here to talk. Let me speak to Patricia."</p>

<p>"She's not taking visitors."</p>

<p>"Tell her I have information about the treatment. Tell her I know how to cure the nanite infection."</p>

<p>The officers exchanged glances. One of them tapped his comm unit and murmured into it. A moment later, the door behind them slid open, and Patricia Okonkwo appeared, dressed in a flight suit, a bag over her shoulder.</p>

<p>"Dr. Vasquez. You have something to tell me?"</p>

<p>"I have a treatment for the nanites. Electromagnetic disruption. It neutralizes them within minutes."</p>

<p>Patricia's eyes narrowed. "Why are you telling me this?"</p>

<p>"Because I want you to know that you failed. The people you tried to destroy are going to live. The colony is going to survive. And you're going to spend the rest of your life running from the consequences of what you've done."</p>

<p>Patricia's face hardened. "You think this is over. It's not. Dorado has resources you can't imagine. They will try again. And next time, they won't make the same mistakes."</p>

<p>"Next time, we'll be ready."</p>

<p>Patricia turned and walked toward the shuttle. Elena raised the sidearm. "Stop. I don't want to shoot you, but I will."</p>

<p>Patricia paused, looking back over her shoulder. "You won't. You're a healer, not a killer."</p>

<p>She was right. Elena's hand trembled. She could not pull the trigger.</p>

<p>Patricia boarded the shuttle. The engines hummed to life. And Elena watched as the woman who had orchestrated the destruction of her colony lifted off from the lunar surface, carrying her secrets into the black void of space.</p>

