<h1 class="chapter-title">11. Earth's Intervention</h1>

<p class="first-para">Governor Marcus Chen listened to his wife's confession in silence, his face a mask of controlled anguish. When she finished, he sat motionless for a long moment, his hands clasped on the desk before him. The only sound in the room was the soft hum of the life-support systems and Li Na's quiet sobbing. Finally, Chen spoke, his voice rough. "You have been working with the people who are killing my colony." "I didn't know—" "You didn't know what? That you were facilitating mass murder? That the information you provided was being used to destroy lives?" He stood abruptly, his chair scraping against the floor. "I have trusted you with everything. My work, my life, my heart. And you have been poisoning all of it." Li Na crumpled, her words lost in tears. Elena stepped forward, placing herself between them. "Governor, we don't have time for this. Patricia Okonkwo is planning to flee in six hours. She has Volkov and the security forces under her control. If we're going to stop her, we need to act now."</p>

<p>Chen's eyes snapped to Elena. "You knew about this? You knew my wife was a traitor?" "I found out twenty minutes ago, the same time you did. And I'm telling you now that we have a limited window to prevent the mastermind of this attack from escaping justice." Chen's jaw worked. He was a man whose entire world had collapsed in the span of minutes, but he was also a leader who had navigated crises before. The politician in him reasserted itself, pushing aside the personal devastation. "If I move against Patricia, I need proof. I need evidence that will hold up to scrutiny." "We have it," Elena said. "The data chip from Clara Morrison. The encrypted messages from Dorado. Anita Kowalski's confession. And now Li Na's testimony." "Li Na's testimony is compromised. She's an admitted conspirator." "Then we use the other evidence. We broadcast it to the entire colony, to Earth, to anyone who will listen. We take away Patricia's ability to hide."</p>

<p>Chen considered. "If we do that, we expose the colony's vulnerabilities. The funding will dry up. The international coalition will fracture." "If we don't do it, Patricia escapes, Dorado wins, and the colony dies anyway." Chen closed his eyes, his shoulders sagging. "I will authorize a transmission to Earth. A direct request for intervention. I will activate the colony's emergency broadcast system." "Patricia will know the moment you do." "Then we do it simultaneously—broadcast to the colony and to Earth at the same time. By the time she reacts, the information will be out of our control." Elena nodded. "I'll get to the communications center. Can you secure it?"</p>

<p>"I'll go with you. My authority still carries weight, even if my trust has been shattered." He looked at his wife, who remained huddled in the corner. "Li Na, you will stay here. Security will be posted at your door. When this is over, we will talk. But not now." They moved swiftly through the executive wing, Chen's presence clearing the path. Colonists and staff alike stepped aside, reading the gravity in his expression. They reached the communications center, a reinforced room at the heart of the colony, and Chen overrode the security protocols with his personal codes. The technician on duty looked up in surprise. "Governor? What's happening?" "We are initiating an emergency broadcast. Priority Alpha. Direct link to Earth command." The technician's eyes widened. Priority Alpha had never been used. "Sir, that will trigger an immediate response from Earth. They'll send an investigation team. They'll—" "I know what it will do. Do it."</p>

<p>The technician's hands flew across the console. "Channel open. You're live in five, four, three—" Chen stepped to the microphone, his voice steady despite everything that had happened. "This is Governor Marcus Chen of Armstrong Central, Lunar Colony. I am activating Priority Alpha protocol. We are under attack. A engineered biological agent has been introduced into our population, resulting in multiple casualties. The attack was orchestrated by a corporate consortium known as Dorado Holdings, operating through agents embedded in our colony. I am requesting immediate Earth intervention. I am requesting an independent investigation. I am requesting medical and security assistance. This is not a drill. This is a call for help." He paused, his voice catching. "And I am accepting full responsibility for the failures of leadership that allowed this to happen."</p>

<p>The transmission ended. The communications center fell silent. Elena watched Chen's face, seeing the weight of his confession settle over him. He had just admitted to the entire world that his colony was compromised, that his leadership had failed. It was the end of his political career. But it was also the beginning of justice. Somewhere in the colony, alarms began to sound. Patricia Okonkwo had heard the broadcast. And she was making her move. Chen turned to Elena, his face pale but resolute. "She'll try to escape immediately. We need to lock down the shuttle bay." "Already on it. But we need a plan. Patricia has security forces loyal to her. We have the truth. That's not an even fight." "Then we make it even. I have people who are still loyal to me. Engineers, medical staff, old friends. We rally them. We hold the line until Earth's team arrives." Elena nodded. It was not much of a plan. But it was the only one they had.</p>

